cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (0.38-2.515 um) Echelle Laser, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic optical, near-infrared YJH, thermal K-band, and simultaneous YJHK
  laser and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures (0.38-2.515 um across ESO HARPS,
  VLT ESPRESSO, ESO NIRPS, VLT CRIRES+, TNG HARPS-N, Calar Alto CARMENES_VIS, CFHT 3.6 m
  SPIRou APERO 0.7.295, and FEROS; 150 unique stars and 1,009 high-resolution echelle
  exposures totaling 195.23 h in V3.0-V4.0 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler, 2D CCD/H2RG/H4RG
  vetoes, sparse G6_V36 coincidence gating, and Channel 5 COMB_V4 matched filtering),
  unified with planetary-rest-frame 1.4 GHz narrowband radio searches (Parkes/GBT) and
  TESS specular light-sail photometry into a 160-system all-sky multi-messenger synthesis.
authors:
  - family-names: "Andersen"
    given-names: "Martin"
version: 0.11.0
date-released: 2026-11-17
repository-code: "https://github.com/andersenmartin-blip/setisearch"
